<% content_for :title, "Registry — Shadwire" %>
<% content_for :description, "The static registry the CLI installs from: index.json, the items with their file contents inlined, and how to serve your own." %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= tag.style rouge_stylesheet %>
<% end %>

<article class="space-y-12">
  <%= render "docs/header",
        title: "Registry",
        description: "Static JSON files served over HTTP, with no application server and no authentication. It is what the CLI reads." %>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <p class="leading-7">
      Shadwire's published registry lives at
      <%= link_to "shadwire.edumoraes.dev.br/r", "https://shadwire.edumoraes.dev.br/r/index.json", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>.
      There are two kinds of document: an index carrying the catalog, and one file per item with
      the contents of each of its files inlined.
    </p>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "URL", "Contents" ],
          rows: [
            [ docs_code("/r/index.json"), "The catalog (name, title, description, when to use) and `base`: the shared files and gems that init installs." ],
            [ docs_code("/r/{name}.json"), "One component: metadata, resolved registry dependencies, the extracted API, and the files with their contents inlined." ],
            [ docs_code("/r/llms.txt"), "The same catalog in plain text, for agents." ],
            [ docs_code("/r/llms-full.txt"), "Every component's full API in plain text." ]
          ] %>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:fetch], language: :shell) %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("index.json") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      What <%= docs_code("list") %> and <%= docs_code("search") %> read, and where
      <%= docs_code("init") %> gets the base installation from.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:index], language: :json) %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("One item") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Each item carries enough to install without a second request, file contents included.
      <%= docs_code("registryDependencies") %> arrives with its transitive closure already
      resolved, so the CLI never has to walk the graph.
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:item], language: :json) %>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Field", "What it is" ],
          rows: [
            [ docs_code("whenToUse"), "One sentence on when to reach for this component and what its neighbours are. It is the text search matches against." ],
            [ docs_code("usage"), "Ready-made ERB snippets for the most common case." ],
            [ docs_code("registryDependencies"), "Other items that have to come along, transitive closure included." ],
            [ docs_code("requiresStimulus"), "True when the item installs a controller under app/javascript/." ],
            [ docs_code("api.components[]"), "Extracted from the source: class, helper, variants, sizes, props and attributes." ],
            [ docs_code("files[]"), safe_join([ "Each file as ", docs_code("{ target, type, content }"), ", with no source paths." ]) ]
          ] %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("How it is built") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The source of truth is <%= docs_code("registry/registry.json") %> in the monorepo, which
      lists each item's files as <%= docs_code("source") %> → <%= docs_code("target") %> pairs.
      <%= docs_code("bin/build_registry") %> turns that into the published registry, inlining the
      contents and extracting the API from the source:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:build], language: :shell) %>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      The output goes to <%= docs_code("build/") %>, which is generated and never hand-edited.
      CI rebuilds it on every push to <%= docs_code("main") %>, alongside this site's deploy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Serving your own") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Because these are static files, any host will do: a bucket, a Pages site, a directory
      behind a proxy. Point the CLI at it with <%= docs_code("--registry") %>, or persist the
      choice into <%= docs_code("shadwire.json") %> by passing the flag to
      <%= docs_code("init") %>.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      <%= docs_code("file://") %> bases work too, which is how you test a registry built locally:
    </p>

    <%= docs_code_block(@snippets[:local], language: :shell) %>

    <%= render layout: "docs/callout", locals: { icon: "triangle-alert", title: "The registry URL is written into the user's app" } do %>
      <code>shadwire.json</code> keeps the URL used at <code>init</code> time. Existing installs
      go on pointing at the old address, so moving a published registry means keeping a
      redirect in place.
    <% end %>
  </section>
</article>
